---------- Forwarded message ----------

I am pleased to announce the release of GNU Ocrad 0.10.

Ocrad is the GNU OCR (Optical Character Recognition) program.

The homepage is at http://www.gnu.org/software/ocrad/ocrad.html.

The sources can be dowloaded from http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/ocrad/ or from
your favorite GNU mirror.

The md5sum is:
84e0cc009bff0572a10772fbcd7101de  ocrad-0.10.tar.bz2

This release is also GPG signed. You can download the signature by
appending ".sig" to the URL.

Changes in version 0.10:

* Added new suboption '-D7X'.
* Change in internal representation; only 1 Blockmap per Textpage.
* Use of absolute coordinates in ORF file. Breaks compatibility with Kooka.
* Improved space detection algorithm.
* Improvements in character recognition and separation.


Please send bug reports and suggestions to <bug-ocrad@gnu.org>.

The test database for Ocrad is growing. I need donations for the purchase of a 
faster computer. Please visit http://www.gnu.org/software/ocrad/ocrad.html and 
make a donation. Thanks.


Regards,
Antonio Diaz, GNU Ocrad author and maintainer.



