iCanProgram (http://www.icanprogram.com/nofeecourses.html) has been 
offering online Linux programming courses for nofees since Jan 2002.     
Students are simply asked to make a voluntary donation to Cancer research 
in memory of one of the course founders.

These courses have been a great success with over 2500 students todate.

iCanProgram would like to extend the reach of these courses to students who 
may not yet have transitioned to Linux.

For this they are actively seeking volunteers from the Knoppix liveCD user 
community to write some online documentation which would allow non Linux 
users to take iCanProgram courses using the Knoppix CD and some form of 
persistent storage (floppy,  memory key).

For more information please peruse the webpage at:
http://www.icanprogram.com/knoppixCD.html

