The SIMPL project (https://sourceforge.net/projects/simpl) aims to bring 
Send/Receive/Reply style messaging first pioneered by RTOS's such as QNX to 
the Linux platform.

After 5 years the SIMPL library is quite mature and widely used.

The project needs to set out on some new directions to keep and capture 
developer interest.

As such they are actively looking for new help to enhance the embedded 
SIMPL offerings (eg.  a port to uClibc for example).

In addition there is need for developers with Knoppix customization skills 
to take the prototype SIMPL selfhosted(live) CD to the finish line.

For more information contact the SIMPL project directly.

